@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g5-senior-inspector.l4: Chapter 5, Subchapter B of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: ss.33 and 34 (the definitions of the Subchapter; the senior inspector;
-- reliance on auxiliary tests and expert opinions; the Mandatory Tenders engagement; the reports of testing
-- bodies and experts; the senior inspector's working rules).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G5.  Imports only prelude and domain.  A fact decided by another provision or another group
-- is an input: that a corporation meets s.35 (g5-testing-bodies), that a person holds an authorisation under
-- s.36 (g5-testing-bodies, g5-withdrawal), the Mandatory Tenders Law (outside the sources).  The definitions of
-- s.33 are BOOLEAN decisions over records of facts; "interested party" (Securities Law) and the Minister's or the
-- senior inspector's judgements are inputs.  Powers are MAY rules guarded by PROVIDED, duties are MUST rules
-- (arising by IF ... ELSE FULFILLED where a condition makes the duty arise), prohibitions are SHANT rules.
-- No period is met in ss.33 and 34: s.34(d), (e) set none (the reports have no time limit in the text).

§ `Chapter 5, Subchapter B: the senior inspector and reliance on auxiliary tests and expert opinions`

§§ `Nouns of ss 33 and 34`

-- The family relationships s.29(a) lists, which s.33 carries over.  A closed list: the Law says "family member
-- means" and lists them.
DECLARE `Family relationship listed in section 29(a)` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse of the subject`
    `a parent of the subject`
    `a parent of a parent of the subject`
    `a son or daughter of the subject`
    `the spouse of a son or daughter of the subject`
    `a brother or sister of the subject`
    `a child of a brother or sister of the subject`
    `a brother-in-law of the subject`
    `a sister-in-law of the subject`
    `an uncle or aunt of the subject`
    `a child of an uncle or aunt of the subject`
    `the subject's wife's father`
    `the subject's wife's mother`
    `the subject's husband's father`
    `the subject's husband's mother`
    `a grandchild of the subject`

DECLARE `How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` HAS
    `family relationship, if the person has one listed` IS A MAYBE `Family relationship listed in section 29(a)`
    `the relationship is by remarriage (a step relationship)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.29(a) "relative", limbs (1) to (4), with the Council member replaced by the tester, expert, testing body,
-- officer or controller (s.33 def.3 "with the necessary changes").  "Interested party" is the Securities Law's.
DECLARE `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` HAS
    `how related` IS A `How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)`                                      -- limb (1)
    `the subject has an interest in the person's economic situation` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- limb (2)
    `a corporation in which the subject, a family member or a person under limb (2) is an interested party` IS A BOOLEAN  -- limb (3)
    `a body in which the subject, a family member or a person under limb (2) is a manager or a responsible employee` IS A BOOLEAN  -- limb (4)

DECLARE `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` HAS
    `the person` IS A `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)`
    `the person's interest or other role conflicts with the subject's function` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.33 def.6: the subject is a tester, an expert, a testing body or its officer or controller.
DECLARE `Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` HAS
    `the subject's own personal interest or other role conflicts with fulfilling his function` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other persons with an interest or role` IS A LIST OF `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)`

-- Facts for s.33 defs 2 and 5.  Whether the authorisation is still in force is decided in ss.36 and 39.
DECLARE `Person who may be a tester or an expert` HAS
    `an employee of a testing body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to carry out auxiliary tests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to give expert opinions` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.33 def.7.
DECLARE `List used in a test under section 33` HAS
    `set by the senior inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set for the carrying out of an auxiliary test` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.33 def.1.
DECLARE `Test under section 33` HAS
    `performed by` IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
    `performed at the requirement of the senior inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `performed on the basis of a list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the list` IS A `List used in a test under section 33`

-- s.33 def.4.
DECLARE `Corporation under section 33` HAS
    `meets the conditions of section 35` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.34(b): what the senior inspector may rely on.
DECLARE `Kind of material under section 34(b)` IS ONE OF
    `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`          -- s.34(b)(1)
    `findings of an auxiliary test done by an expert`         -- s.34(b)(2)
    `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`   -- s.34(b)(2)

DECLARE `Material offered to the senior inspector` HAS
    `kind of material` IS A `Kind of material under section 34(b)`
    `the test` IS A `Test under section 33`
    `the expert who gave the opinion` IS A MAYBE `Person who may be a tester or an expert`   -- NOTHING unless the material is an opinion
    `for supervising the implementation of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Candidate for authorisation as the senior inspector` HAS
    `an inspector authorised by the Minister under section 30(a)` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)` HAS
    `made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)` HAS
    `covers an auxiliary test and its findings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the manager of the testing body` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Report by an expert under section 34(e)` HAS
    `covers an auxiliary test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives the expert's opinion on the results` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the expert` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Position of an expert under section 34(e)` HAS
    `engaged in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by a testing body` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `An act under sections 33 and 34` IS ONE OF
    `authorise an inspector as the senior inspector`
        HAS `the inspector authorised` IS A `Candidate for authorisation as the senior inspector`
    `rely on material from an auxiliary test`
        HAS `the material relied on` IS A `Material offered to the senior inspector`
    `engage a testing body or an expert for reliance`
        HAS `the engagement made` IS AN `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)`
    `report an auxiliary test and its findings`
        HAS `the report made` IS A `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)`
    `report an auxiliary test and give an opinion on its results`
        HAS `the expert's report made` IS A `Report by an expert under section 34(e)`
    `act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs`

§§ `s 33 -- Definitions of the Subchapter`

-- src:269 | {{ח:סעיף|33|הגדרות – {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן ב|סימן ב׳}}}}
-- src:270 | {{ח:ת}} {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן ב|בסימן זה}} –
-- The lead-in introduces seven definitions that each have their own rule below; it has no content of its own
-- (coverage row s.33: inert).

-- src:271 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בדיקת עזר“ – בדיקה המבוצעת בידי בודק או מומחה, לפי דרישת המפקח הבכיר, על פי רשימת תיוג בדבר התקיימות התנאים המנויים ברשימת התיוג;
-- def.1, "auxiliary test": by a tester or expert, at the senior inspector's requirement, on the basis of a
-- checklist.  The closing words, "concerning the fulfilment of the conditions listed in the checklist", only
-- describe what a checklist is for and add no condition.
@ref s.33 lead-in, def.1 (src:269-270, src:271)
GIVEN performer IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 1 — the performer is a tester or an expert` performer MEANS
        `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` performer
    OR  `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` performer

@ref s.33 def.1 (src:271)
GIVEN test IS A `Test under section 33`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` test MEANS
        "by a tester or an expert" ... `s 33 def 1 — the performer is a tester or an expert` (test's `performed by`)
    AND "at the senior inspector's requirement" ... test's `performed at the requirement of the senior inspector`
    AND "on the basis of a checklist" ... test's `performed on the basis of a list`
    AND "checklist" ... `s 33 def 7 — the list is a checklist` (test's `the list`)

-- src:272 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בודק“ – עובד גוף בודק שהשר הסמיכו לבצע בדיקות עזר לשם סיוע למפקח הבכיר, לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 36|סעיף 36}};
-- def.2, "tester": an employee of a testing body whom the Minister authorised under s.36 to carry out auxiliary
-- tests to assist the senior inspector.  Whether that authorisation is in force is a question of ss.36 and 39.
@ref s.33 def.2 (src:272)
@export Whether a person is a tester within s.33 of the Law: an employee of a testing body whom the Minister authorised under s.36 to carry out auxiliary tests
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert` @desc The person: whether he is employed by a testing body or engaged to be relied on, and which authorisations under s.36 he holds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` person MEANS
        person's `an employee of a testing body`
    AND person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to carry out auxiliary tests`

-- src:273 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בן משפחה“ ו”קרוב“, של בודק, של מומחה או של גוף בודק או נושא משרה או בעל שליטה בו – כהגדרתם {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 29|בסעיף 29(א)}}, בשינויים המחויבים;
-- def.3: "family member" and "relative" of a tester, expert, testing body, or an officer or controller of one,
-- are as in s.29(a), with the necessary changes.  The text of s.29(a) follows (lines 230 and 234 to 238), read
-- here with the subject changed from a Council member.
-- src:230 | {{ח:תת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בן משפחה“ – בן זוג, הורה, הורה הורה, בן או בת ובני זוגם, אח או אחות וילדיהם, גיס, גיסה, דוד או דודה וילדיהם, חותן, חותנת, חם, חמות, נכד או נכדה, לרבות קרוב כאמור שהוא שלוב (חורג);
-- src:234 | {{ח:תת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”קרוב“, של חבר המועצה – כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:235 | {{ח:תתתת|(1)}} בן משפחה של חבר המועצה;
-- src:236 | {{ח:תתתת|(2)}} אדם שלחבר המועצה יש עניין במצבו הכלכלי;
-- src:237 | {{ח:תתתת|(3)}} תאגיד שחבר המועצה, בן משפחתו או אדם כאמור בפסקה (2) הם בעלי עניין בו;
-- src:238 | {{ח:תתתת|(4)}} גוף שחבר המועצה, בן משפחתו או אדם כאמור בפסקה (2) הם מנהלים או עובדים אחראים בו.
-- "Family member" is a closed list; a step relative, which the closing words of src:230 include, is included, so the step flag changes nothing.
@ref s.33 def.3; s.29(a) "family member" (src:273, src:230)
GIVEN how IS A `How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` how MEANS
    CONSIDER how's `family relationship, if the person has one listed`
    WHEN JUST relationship THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- "Relative", limbs (1) to (4): a family member; a person in whose economic situation the subject has an
-- interest; a corporation in which the subject, a family member or a limb (2) person is an interested party; a
-- body in which they are managers or responsible employees.
@ref s.33 def.3; s.29(a) "relative" (src:273, src:234-238)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` person MEANS
        "(1)" ... `s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` (person's `how related`)
    OR  "(2)" ... person's `the subject has an interest in the person's economic situation`
    OR  "(3)" ... person's `a corporation in which the subject, a family member or a person under limb (2) is an interested party`
    OR  "(4)" ... person's `a body in which the subject, a family member or a person under limb (2) is a manager or a responsible employee`

-- src:274 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”גוף בודק“ – תאגיד שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 35|סעיף 35}} ובוצעה עימו התקשרות לשם הסתייעות בו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|סעיף 34(ב)}};
-- def.4, "testing body": a corporation that meets s.35 and with which an engagement was made to rely on it under
-- s.34(b).  Whether it meets s.35 is decided by g5-testing-bodies (`s 35 — the corporation may serve as a
-- testing body`) and arrives here as an input.
@ref s.33 def.4 (src:274)
GIVEN corporation IS A `Corporation under section 33`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 4 — the corporation is a testing body` corporation MEANS
        corporation's `meets the conditions of section 35`
    AND corporation's `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)`

-- src:275 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מומחה“ – עובד גוף בודק או מי שבוצעה עימו התקשרות לשם הסתייעות בו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|סעיף 34(ב)}}, שהשר הסמיכו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 36|סעיף 36}} לבצע בדיקות עזר או לתת חוות דעת מומחה, לפי העניין;
-- def.5, "expert": an employee of a testing body, or a person engaged to be relied on under s.34(b), whom the
-- Minister authorised under s.36 to carry out auxiliary tests or to give expert opinions "as the case may be".
-- Read literally the definition overlaps def.2: an employee authorised only to test is both a tester and an
-- expert (fork F-OVERLAP; see FRAGMENT-G5.md, contradictions).  The literal reading is taken; the alternative
-- that keeps an employee authorised only to test out of the experts follows.
@ref s.33 def.5 (src:275)
@export Whether a person is an expert within s.33 of the Law: an employee of a testing body or a person engaged to be relied on, whom the Minister authorised under s.36 to carry out auxiliary tests or to give expert opinions
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert` @desc The person: whether he is employed by a testing body or engaged to be relied on, and which authorisations under s.36 he holds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` person MEANS
        (    person's `an employee of a testing body`
         OR  person's `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)` )
    AND (    person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to carry out auxiliary tests`
         OR  person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to give expert opinions` )

@ref s.33 def.5 (src:275)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` person MEANS
        (    person's `an employee of a testing body`
         AND person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to give expert opinions` )
    OR  (    person's `engaged to be relied on under section 34(b)`
         AND (    person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to carry out auxiliary tests`
              OR  person's `authorised by the Minister under section 36 to give expert opinions` ) )

-- src:276 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”ניגוד עניינים“, של בודק, של מומחה או של גוף בודק – ניגוד עניינים בין מילוי תפקידו של הבודק, המומחה או הגוף הבודק או של נושא משרה או בעל שליטה בו, לפי העניין, לבין עניין אישי או תפקיד אחר, שלו או של קרובו;
-- def.6, "conflict of interest" of a tester, expert or testing body (or its officer or controller, "as the case
-- may be"): a conflict between fulfilling his function and a personal interest or other role of his OR of a
-- relative's.  Whether an interest or role conflicts is a judgement and an input; whether a person is a relative
-- is def.3.
@ref s.33 def.6 (src:276)
GIVEN other IS AN `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 6 — the other person is a relative whose interest or role conflicts with the subject's function` other MEANS
        `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` (other's `the person`)
    AND other's `the person's interest or other role conflicts with the subject's function`

@ref s.33 def.6 (src:276)
@export Whether a tester, expert or testing body (or an officer or controller of one) is in a conflict of interest within s.33 of the Law: his function conflicts with a personal interest or other role of his own or of a relative
GIVEN situation IS A `Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` @desc His own interests and roles, and those of other persons with how each is related to him
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` situation MEANS
        situation's `the subject's own personal interest or other role conflicts with fulfilling his function`
    OR  any `s 33 def 6 — the other person is a relative whose interest or role conflicts with the subject's function` (situation's `other persons with an interest or role`)

-- src:277 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”רשימת תיוג“ – רשימה שקבע המפקח הבכיר לשם ביצוע בדיקת עזר, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 37|בסעיף 37(א)(3)}}.
-- def.7, "checklist": a list the senior inspector set to carry out an auxiliary test, as s.37(a)(3) says.
@ref s.33 def.7 (src:277)
GIVEN list IS A `List used in a test under section 33`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33 def 7 — the list is a checklist` list MEANS
        list's `set by the senior inspector`
    AND list's `set for the carrying out of an auxiliary test`

§§ `s 34 -- The senior inspector, and reliance on auxiliary tests and expert opinions`

-- src:279 | {{ח:סעיף|34|מפקח בכיר והסתייעות בבדיקות עזר ובחוות דעת מומחה}}
-- src:280 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר יסמיך, מקרב המפקחים, מפקח בכיר שיהיו נתונות לו, נוסף על הסמכויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן א|סימן א׳}}, גם הסמכויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ה סימן ב|סימן זה}}.
-- s.34(a) reads "the Minister will authorise" (the verb at src:280): taken as a duty, as in s.30(a) (fork F-DUTY).
@ref s.34(a) (src:280)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(a) — the Minister shall authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST  `authorise an inspector as the senior inspector` authorisee
          PROVIDED authorisee's `an inspector authorised by the Minister under section 30(a)`

@ref s.34(a) (src:280)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `authorise an inspector as the senior inspector` authorisee
          PROVIDED authorisee's `an inspector authorised by the Minister under section 30(a)`

-- src:281 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} לשם פיקוח על ביצוע ההוראות לפי חוק זה, רשאי המפקח הבכיר להסתייע באלה:
-- src:282 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} ממצאים של בדיקות עזר שביצע בודק;
-- src:283 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} ממצאים של בדיקות עזר שביצע מומחה וכן חוות דעת שנתן מומחה לגבי תוצאות הבדיקה כאמור ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ה|בפרק זה}} – חוות דעת מומחה).
-- s.34(b): the senior inspector may rely on (1) findings of auxiliary tests by a tester, (2) findings of
-- auxiliary tests by an expert and an expert's opinion on their results, to supervise implementation of the Law.
-- Only an auxiliary test (def.1) will do: a test not made at his requirement on a checklist is not one.
@ref s.34(b)(2) (src:283)
GIVEN giver IS A MAYBE `Person who may be a tester or an expert`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(b)(2) — the opinion was given by an expert` giver MEANS
    CONSIDER giver
    WHEN JUST expert THEN `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` expert
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN FALSE

@ref s.34(b)(1), (2) (src:282-283)
GIVEN material IS A `Material offered to the senior inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(b) — the material is findings by a tester, or findings or an opinion by an expert` material MEANS
    CONSIDER material's `kind of material`
    WHEN `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`
        THEN `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` (material's `the test`'s `performed by`)
    WHEN `findings of an auxiliary test done by an expert`
        THEN `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` (material's `the test`'s `performed by`)
    WHEN `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`
        THEN    `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` (material's `the test`'s `performed by`)
            AND `s 34(b)(2) — the opinion was given by an expert` (material's `the expert who gave the opinion`)

@ref s.34(b) (src:281-283)
GIVEN material IS A `Material offered to the senior inspector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` material MEANS
        "lead-in" ... material's `for supervising the implementation of the Law`
    AND "auxiliary test" ... `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` (material's `the test`)
    AND "(1), (2)" ... `s 34(b) — the material is findings by a tester, or findings or an opinion by an expert` material

@ref s.34(b) (src:281-283)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on auxiliary test findings and expert opinions` MEANS
    PARTY `the senior inspector`
    MAY   `rely on material from an auxiliary test` offered
          PROVIDED `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` offered

-- src:284 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} התקשרות עם גוף בודק או עם מומחה לשם הסתייעות בו כאמור בסעיף קטן (ב), תיעשה לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק חובת המכרזים|חוק חובת המכרזים, התשנ״ב–1992}}; ואולם אין באמור כדי לגרוע מהאפשרות כי המומחה יועסק על ידי גוף בודק.
-- s.34(c): the engagement of a testing body or an expert to be relied on "shall be made under" the Mandatory
-- Tenders Law, whose text is outside the sources: that an engagement was so made is an input.  The text names no
-- engaging party; the Ministry (the State acting through the Minister's office, s.2 "the Ministry") is inferred
-- (fork F-ACTOR) and is the PARTY of the prohibition below.  "Shall be made under" is read as: no engagement
-- except under that Law, hence SHANT, guarded by the negated condition.
-- The last words ("nothing derogates from the possibility that the expert be employed by a testing body") do not
-- add a rule: an expert employed by a testing body is an expert under def.5, and the tests assert it
-- (avoidance of doubt, phrasebook 10.1).
@ref s.34(c) (src:284)
GIVEN engagement IS AN `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(c) — the engagement is made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` engagement MEANS
    engagement's `made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law`

@ref s.34(c) (src:284)
GIVEN engager IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(c) — a testing body or an expert shall be engaged to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law, the party engaging being` engager MEANS
    PARTY engager
    SHANT `engage a testing body or an expert for reliance` engaged
          PROVIDED NOT `s 34(c) — the engagement is made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` engaged
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY engager BECAUSE "s 34(c): a testing body or an expert was engaged to be relied on otherwise than in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law"

@ref s.34(c) (src:284)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(c) — the Ministry shall engage a testing body or an expert to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` MEANS
    `s 34(c) — a testing body or an expert shall be engaged to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law, the party engaging being` `the Ministry`

-- src:285 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} גוף בודק שבוצעה עימו התקשרות בהתאם להוראות סעיף קטן (ג), ידווח למפקח הבכיר על כל בדיקת עזר שביצע ועל ממצאיה; הדיווח ייחתם בידי מנהל הגוף הבודק.
-- s.34(d): a testing body "with which an engagement was made in accordance with (c)" shall report each auxiliary
-- test it performed and its findings to the senior inspector; the report is signed by the body's manager.  The
-- duty arises only for a body engaged under (c); a body engaged otherwise is outside it (the G5 fork on s.34(c)).
-- No time is stated for the report, so none is written.
@ref s.34(d) (src:285)
GIVEN engagement IS AN `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(d) — an engaged testing body shall report each auxiliary test and its findings to the senior inspector` engagement MEANS
    IF   `s 34(c) — the engagement is made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` engagement
    THEN PARTY `a testing body`
         MUST  `report an auxiliary test and its findings` reported
               PROVIDED `s 34(d) — the report covers the auxiliary test and its findings and is signed by the manager` reported
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `a testing body` BECAUSE "s 34(d): the engaged testing body did not report an auxiliary test and its findings, signed by its manager"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.34(d) (src:285)
GIVEN report IS A `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(d) — the report covers the auxiliary test and its findings and is signed by the manager` report MEANS
        report's `covers an auxiliary test and its findings`
    AND report's `signed by the manager of the testing body`

-- src:286 | {{ח:תת|(ה)}} מומחה שבוצעה עימו התקשרות בהתאם להוראות סעיף קטן (ג) או המועסק על ידי גוף בודק, ידווח למפקח הבכיר על כל בדיקת עזר שביצע ויחווה את דעתו על תוצאות הבדיקה; הדיווח וחוות הדעת ייחתמו בידי המומחה.
-- s.34(e): an expert engaged under (c) OR employed by a testing body shall report each auxiliary test he
-- performed and give his opinion on its results; the report and the opinion are signed by the expert.  An
-- employed expert is bound although no engagement of his own was made (contrast (d) and ss.38(a), 38(c)).
@ref s.34(e) (src:286)
GIVEN position IS A `Position of an expert under section 34(e)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(e) — the expert is engaged in accordance with section 34(c) or employed by a testing body` position MEANS
        position's `engaged in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law`
    OR  position's `employed by a testing body`

@ref s.34(e) (src:286)
GIVEN report IS A `Report by an expert under section 34(e)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` report MEANS
        report's `covers an auxiliary test`
    AND report's `gives the expert's opinion on the results`
    AND report's `signed by the expert`

@ref s.34(e) (src:286)
GIVEN position IS A `Position of an expert under section 34(e)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` position MEANS
    IF   `s 34(e) — the expert is engaged in accordance with section 34(c) or employed by a testing body` position
    THEN PARTY `an expert`
         MUST  `report an auxiliary test and give an opinion on its results` reported
               PROVIDED `s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` reported
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `an expert` BECAUSE "s 34(e): the expert did not report an auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results, signed by him"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:287 | {{ח:תת|(ו)}} בודקים ומומחים יפעלו לפי כללי עבודה כפי שיורה המפקח הבכיר.
-- s.34(f): testers and experts "will act" under working rules as the senior inspector directs.  The content of
-- the rules is the senior inspector's; compliance is the act.  The party is a parameter so one rule serves both
-- (the headline rules fix it to a tester and to an expert).
@ref s.34(f) (src:287)
GIVEN who IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(f) — a tester or an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs, the party bound being` who MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST  `act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY who BECAUSE "s 34(f): the working rules the senior inspector directed were not followed"

@ref s.34(f) (src:287)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(f) — a tester shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` MEANS
    `s 34(f) — a tester or an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs, the party bound being` `a tester`

@ref s.34(f) (src:287)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under sections 33 and 34`
`s 34(f) — an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` MEANS
    `s 34(f) — a tester or an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs, the party bound being` `an expert`

-- src:303 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} השר רשאי להורות בכתב ההסמכה על תנאים והוראות לעניין דרכי פעולתו וסדרי עבודתו של בודק או של מומחה, ובכלל זה לפי סוגים של בדיקות עזר שהוא מוסמך לבצע, ורשאי הוא לשנות תנאים והוראות שנתן לעניין דרכי פעולתו לאחר שניתנה לבודק או למומחה הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו בכתב.
-- s.34(f) lets the senior inspector direct working rules for testers and experts; s.36(d) (line 303 above) lets the
-- Minister direct conditions and instructions on their modes of action and work procedures in the instrument of
-- authorisation.  The two overlap, and neither section says which prevails if they conflict (fork F-OVERLAP-RULES,
-- FRAGMENT-G5.md, contradictions).  The sources do not answer, so the answer is a named refusal, not a default.
@ref s.34(f); s.36(d) (src:287, src:303)
GIVETH A Party
`s 34(f), s 36(d) — the party whose rule governs when the instrument of authorisation and the senior inspector's working rules conflict` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 34(f), s 36(d) — the party whose rule governs when the instrument of authorisation and the senior inspector's working rules conflict"
